,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Summary\r\n\r\nWhen configuring colors using environment variables, streamlit returns an error message upon page load.\r\n\r\n```\r\nBad message format\r\nFailed to parse color: \"#FFFFFF \"\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt somehow seems to include a space at the end of the color string. However the code snippet below clearly shows there is no space in the environment variable.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nThis is the bash file that I used to launch streamlit\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nexport STREAMLIT_THEME_PRIMARY_COLOR=\"#EA650E\"\r\nexport STREAMLIT_THEME_SECONDARY_BACKGROUND_COLOR=\"#F8F8F8\"\r\nexport STREAMLIT_THEME_BACKGROUND_COLOR=\"#FFFFFF\"\r\nexport STREAMLIT_THEME_TEXT_COLOR=\"#000000\"\r\nexport STREAMLIT_THEME_FONT=\"sans serif\"\r\nstreamlit run app.py --server.enableWebsocketCompression=false --server.enableXsrfProtection=false &\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior:**\r\n\r\nI expected a working streamlit page with my colors applied\r\n\r\n**Actual behavior:**\r\n\r\nReceived modal with error message upon page load:\r\n\r\n```\r\nBad message format\r\nFailed to parse color: \"#FFFFFF \"\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Is this a regression?\r\n\r\nDon't know, have not tried this before\r\n\r\n### Debug info\r\n\r\n- Streamlit version: 0.80.0\r\n- Python version: 3.7\r\n- Using Conda\r\n- OS version: Ubuntu 20.04\r\n- Browser version: Viewing on Windows 10, Chrome 89.0.4389.114 \r\n\r\n### Additional information\r\n\r\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"iiLaurens","id":9915637,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5MTU2Mzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9915637?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiLaurens","html_url":"https://github.com/iiLaurens","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiLaurens/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiLaurens/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiLaurens/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiLaurens/st